; --- anxnet.device, anxgenet.device, anxzz9000.device and anxwifipi.device -----------------
;
; Why it is not a question is at DO_ANXNET in section 4.
;
; DEVS:Networks/, NOT DEVS:.  That is the SANA-II convention, it is where
; P_dev_path looks second and what DEVICE=DEVS:Networks/anxnet.device names,
; and the drawer does not exist on a stock Workbench -- hence the makedir,
; which is unconditional inside the yes for the same reason the two in section
; 6 are: it is content with a drawer that is already there.
;
; THE OLD ONE IS RENAMED ASIDE, the way bsdsocket.library and tls.library are
; above, and for both of their reasons: a driver that is open cannot be copied
; over, and somebody whose network stops working after an update needs the
; previous driver still on the disk.  A .old left by an earlier run goes first,
; so the rename never fails onto a name that is already taken.
;
; One build of it, like everything else in the archive.  There is nothing to
; choose between: no AMINETXDUO_* feature flag reaches src/netdev, so the
; minimal build compiles the same driver, and dist/make-dist.sh stages it once
; at the top of Devs/Networks/ rather than once per stack.

